Decided: a lane-failed-start is void once the lane logs a turn-end after it, so a gone lane that reported working takes the existing respawn path
Because: "A `lane-dead` (or a hibernated lane gone) on an impl/fix lane in `working` makes drive respawn it in the next pass"
Rejected: a new respawn branch for hibernated lanes — the existing gone-lane respawn (30 min pacing, LANE_ENDS after two, RESPAWN_LOOP) already covers it; only the stale failed start hid it
Decided: this fleet's own queue blockers are read on GitHub like other repos' ones; a closed one logs blocker-closed and drops out of the queue view
Because: "A blocker closed not-planned no longer holds its dependants, and an event says so (test)."
Decided: queue add refuses IS_PR when the issue view's url is a /pull/ one; the spec read now asks for url
Because: "`queue add <n>` where `<n>` is a PR is refused with a clear code (test)."
Decided: a gone lane whose issue is held shows "held by #N" on the Lanes and Queue tabs instead of dead or parked
Because: "On the board, a held lane shows as held by its blocker, not dead."
Decided: the Queue tab skips a row whose cached issue view is a pull request
Check: an issue spec cached before this change has no url, so an already-queued PR number (#828, #832) drops off only once its spec is read again, or by queue rm
Owner: A lane that said it was still working and then vanished is now restarted automatically, and the board stops calling held lanes dead.
